# ASI: GgufLoader

## Finding: G1 loader was hardcoded stub

```yaml
g1_audit_result:
  file:    "brain/master/src/provider/gguf/loader.rs"
  finding: |
    BrainGgufLoader::verify() returned hardcoded:
      { architecture: "qwen2", tensors: 291, vocab: 151936 }
    regardless of actual file path.
  detection: "python3 audit/scripts/gguf_verify.py --stub-check"
  fix_status: UNVERIFIED  # loader grew 1.07->1.92KB on 2026-06-06T12:11
                          # Cargo.toml only grew 20 bytes â€” no hacedle dep added
  risk: |
    If loader.rs added inline parsing rather than delegating to hacedle::GgufLoaderStd,
    this is a S-05 reuse violation AND creates a second diverging GGUF parser.
```

---

## Mandatory delegation rule

```yaml
rule: "brain/master GgufLoader MUST delegate to hacedle â€” MUST NOT parse inline"
rationale: |
  fem/hacedle/src/x/loader/gguf/ already provides:
    loader_std.rs   2.31KB â€” GgufLoaderStd::load(path) -> GgufFile
    header.rs       1.87KB â€” parse magic, version, tensor_count, kv_count
    tensor_index.rs 3.68KB â€” TensorIndex::build() -> name->offset map
    tensor_view.rs  1.20KB â€” TensorView for lazy slice access
    mmap.rs         0.38KB â€” MmapFile for memory-mapped access
    model_spec.rs   1.89KB â€” ModelSpec { hidden_size, n_heads, n_kv_heads, ffn_dim }
    quant_router.rs 0.96KB â€” GGML type routing

  Total hacedle GGUF assets: ~12.4KB, battle-tested, no_std compatible.
  A second inline parser in brain/master = dead weight + divergence risk.

correct_impl: |
  // brain/master/src/provider/gguf/loader.rs
  use hace_fem_hacedle::x::loader::gguf::loader_std::GgufLoaderStd;
  use hace_fem_hacedle::x::loader::gguf::tensor_index::TensorIndex;
  use hace_fem_hacedle::x::loader::gguf::model_spec::ModelSpec;

  pub struct GgufLoader;

  impl GgufLoader {
      pub fn load(path: &str) -> Result<LoadedModel, GgufError> {
          let file    = GgufLoaderStd::open(path)
              .map_err(|e| GgufError::IoError(e.to_string()))?;
          let index   = TensorIndex::build(&file)
              .map_err(|e| GgufError::ParseError(e.to_string()))?;
          let spec    = ModelSpec::from_metadata(&file.metadata)
              .unwrap_or_default();
          Ok(LoadedModel { file, tensor_index: index, model_spec: spec })
      }
  }
```

---

## LoadedModel contract

```yaml
struct LoadedModel:
  fields:
    file:         "GgufLoaderStd â€” owns file handle + mmap"
    tensor_index: "TensorIndex   â€” name -> TensorEntry { offset, dims, qtype }"
    model_spec:   "ModelSpec     â€” hidden_size, n_layers, n_kv_heads, head_dim, vocab_size"
  
  access_pattern: |
    // Lazy: tensor data NOT loaded until explicitly accessed
    let entry  = model.tensor_index.lookup("blk.0.attn_q.weight")?;
    let slice  = model.file.mmap_slice(entry.offset, entry.byte_len())?;
    let dequant = hacedle::x::loader::dequant::q4_k::dequant_q4_k(slice, dims);
```

---

## IPO contract

```yaml
input:
  I1: "path: &str â€” absolute or relative path to *.gguf file"
  I2: "options: LoadOptions { max_tensor_ram_mb: usize }"  # E4 default: 512MB guard

process:
  P1: "open file, read 4-byte magic, assert == b'GGUF'"
  P2: "parse header: version u32, tensor_count u64, kv_count u64"
  P3: "parse kv metadata: architecture, context_length, block_count, vocab..."
  P4: "build TensorIndex: iterate tensor_count entries, store name->offset"
  P5: "memory-map file for lazy tensor access (no eager load)"

output:
  O1: "LoadedModel { file, tensor_index, model_spec }"

errors:
  GgufError::NotFound:           "path does not exist â€” check before open"
  GgufError::BadMagic:           "first 4 bytes != GGUF â€” include actual hex in message"
  GgufError::UnsupportedVersion: "version > 3 â€” emit version number"
  GgufError::OomRisk:            "estimated tensor RAM > options.max_tensor_ram_mb"
  GgufError::ParseError:         "malformed KV or tensor table â€” include byte offset"
  
  no_panic: true   # all errors returned via Result, never panic!
```

---

## Cargo.toml requirement

```toml
# brain/master/Cargo.toml â€” REQUIRED for delegation
[dependencies]
hace-fem-hacedle = { path = "../../../../fem/hacedle",
                     default-features = false,
                     features = ["alloc", "gguf-loader"] }
```

